# Root line-ending policy. TASK-0034 follow-up (STATE.md open question 6, 2026-09-07).
#
# Why this file exists: `backend/.gitattributes` normalised `backend/**` only, so everything
# outside it — `contracts/`, `frontend/`, `.agent/`, root CI and docs — fell through to whatever
# `core.autocrlf` happened to be on each machine. Nothing in the repo is STORED with CRLF (every
# tracked text file is `i/lf`), so this file changes no committed content; what it fixes is the
# WORKTREE, which until now was LF on this machine only because generators wrote those files
# rather than a checkout.
#
# The concrete failure it prevents: `contracts/openapi.json`, `contracts/CONTRACT.lock` and
# `frontend/src/api/schema.d.ts` are compared BYTE-FOR-BYTE by the drift gates — ci.ps1 gate 10
# hashes the contract with Get-FileHash, and `npm run check:api-drift` string-compares the
# generated client. On a fresh clone on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, git would hand all three
# out as CRLF, and both gates would fail on line endings alone while CI (ubuntu-latest) stayed
# green. That is the same class of bug as TASK-0034 itself, one layer out: a byte-exact gate is
# only as good as the bytes being reproducible.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows shell scripts must keep CRLF — cmd.exe mis-parses LF line continuations.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# GENERATED ARTEFACTS, hashed byte-for-byte by the drift gates (CLAUDE.md §4.4 checks 1, 2 and 4).
# Covered by `* text=auto eol=lf` above; named explicitly anyway, because a future edit that
# loosens the blanket rule must not silently take these with it.
contracts/openapi.json        text eol=lf
contracts/CONTRACT.lock       text eol=lf
frontend/src/api/schema.d.ts  text eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.dll  binary
*.exe  binary
*.pfx  binary
*.snk  binary

# Diff/merge hints.
*.json text
*.md   text
*.sln  text eol=crlf

# NOTE: `backend/.gitattributes` still exists and still wins for paths under `backend/` (a
# subdirectory .gitattributes takes precedence). It repeats `* text=auto eol=lf` and the binary
# list, which is harmless because the two agree exactly; its .NET-specific hints (`*.cs
# diff=csharp`, `*.csproj merge=union`, `*.slnx`) are its own and belong there. Consolidating the
# duplicated lines is a backend-owned tidy-up, not a correctness issue.
